/**
 * requestFacets.heldout4.spec.ts — fourth held-out facet set (eval-0927 P0-2).
 * 80 items (40 EN + 40 JA; 52 positives, 28 hard negatives) generated by
 * EVO-X2 in a fresh context (2026-09-27) over fifteen more domains (IMAP
 * sync, slicers, dispatch, POS, dependency resolvers, browser extensions,
 * chat servers, photo filters, log pipelines, autocomplete, recurrence
 * rules, PDF rendering, backups, telematics, ticketing); at least a third of
 * the positives avoid the facet's obvious keyword, and the negatives include
 * direction traps ("what does X import" asks for X's own dependencies).
 * Labels adjudicated by the orchestrator BEFORE any scoring ("max N before
 * it gives up", "step by step how X decides", "when X hits the budget, what
 * is cut in what order": condition tolerated).
 *
 * Scored BLIND twice: the FIX-C1 extractor (recall value 0.50 / condition
 * 0.44 / callers 0.38 / flow 0.06, 2/28 negatives with a facet) and the
 * second generalization (0.56 / 0.67 / 0.81 / 0.38, 4/28); then used as a
 * DEVELOPMENT set for the third generalization, with a fifth unseen set as
 * the final blind check. This file only SCORES; it must never gain an
 * item-specific branch.
 */
